  "id": "drug-induced-parkinsonism",
  "term": "drug-induced parkinsonism",
  "definition": "Drug-induced parkinsonism is a movement disorder caused by antipsychotic medication and is the most common movement problem linked to these drugs. It usually affects both sides of the body similarly, although some people show unequal involvement from one side to the other.",
